      "id": "be-s6-att-pricing-examples-c1",
      "heading": "Example 1: raise or lower the price?",
      "explanation_md": "A report gives **AT&T's own price elasticity of demand for long distance services as -8.64**. AT&T needs to **boost revenues**. Should it raise or lower its price?\n\n**Answer: lower the price.** |-8.64| is greater than 1, so demand is **elastic**. A price cut makes quantity demanded rise by a **greater percentage than the price fell**, so revenue goes up.",
