      "id": "be-s6-att-pricing-examples-c3",
      "heading": "Example 3: a competitor cuts its price",
      "explanation_md": "A report gives AT&T's **cross price elasticity of demand as 9.06**. If **competitors reduce prices by 4%**, what happens to demand for AT&T services?\n\n9.06 = %ΔQ / (-4%)\n\n%ΔQ = (-4%) x 9.06 = **-36.24%**\n\nAT&T's demand **falls by 36.24 percent**. The cross elasticity is positive, so the services are **substitutes**.",
      "example_ids": [
        "be-ex-s6-att-cross"
      ],
