    {
      "id": "be-s6-att-pricing-examples-q-6b695551",
      "type": "long",
      "stem": "Differentiate between the effect of own price elasticity and cross price elasticity on a firm's demand, using the AT&T figures.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "**Introduction.** Own price elasticity reacts to the firm's own price; cross price elasticity reacts to another firm's price.\n\n| Point | Own price | Cross price |\n|---|---|---|\n| Value | -8.64 | 9.06 |\n| Price change | Own price down 3% | Competitors' price down 4% |\n| Effect on AT&T | Calls up 25.92% | Demand down 36.24% |\n| Sign meaning | Law of demand, elastic | Substitutes |\n\n**Conclusion.** One gives the firm's own pricing lever, the other the risk from rivals.",
      "rubric": [
